+# Do not delete files in this directory
+
+`jobs/<id>.json` is not a cache or a temp file. It is written by `accept.py`
+the moment an upload is accepted and removed by `worker.py` only after the
+thumbnails are rendered and the CDN is purged. Between those two points it is
+the **only** record that the upload happened.
+
+A cleanup script that deleted these by age (older than an hour) while the
+worker was mid-drain cost eleven customers their uploads; they had to be
+emailed and asked to re-upload. Age is not a signal here -- a job can sit
+legitimately while the worker is down or backed up.
+
+Files named `.<id>.tmp` are partial writes from `accept.py` and are renamed
+into place immediately. Only these are safe to reap, and only if their mtime
+is old enough that no `accept()` call can still be in flight.
